# Deny-all, then re-admit exactly what the build stage needs (`npm ci` +
# `next build`, which traces app/components/lib/data/public for the
# `standalone` output). Chosen over an allow-all-except form (this file's
# prior shape) because that form leaks anything new dropped at repo root by
# default — which is exactly how .zitadel-data/*.pat (Zitadel admin/login
# PATs) and .stack-out/cdcf-infra (a full git clone) ended up copied into a
# build-stage layer via `COPY . .`. Mirrors martyrology-api's .dockerignore.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!next.config.ts
!next-env.d.ts
!postcss.config.mjs
!eslint.config.mjs
!app
!components
!lib
!data
!public
